{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.UnitaryGroup","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Spectrum"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit_orbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit_orbit","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L170-L271","doc":"**Lemma** ([`lem:fai-projector-coadjoint-orbit`], coadjoint-orbit\nhalf) — **proved sorry-free**.\n\nThe traceless component `σ(ρ) = ρ − ½·id_V` of every rank-1\nprojector on the categorical-dimension-2 standard representation —\narchimedean realisation: a Hermitian idempotent of trace 1 on\n`τ(V) = ℂ²` — is unitarily conjugate to the single base point\n`σ₀ = ½·diag(1, −1)`.  Hence the `σ`-image of `ℙ(V)` is one\n`U(2)`-adjoint orbit, and `σ` identifies\n`ℙ(V) ≅ G/T = U(2)/(U(1) × U(1))` with a closed coadjoint orbit in\n`Ad(A)` (the `.md` lemma's second half).\n\nProof (spectral theorem, no `sorry`).  By `Matrix.IsHermitian.spectral_theorem`,\n`ρ = U · diagonal(eigenvalues) · U⋆` with `U` unitary, so\n`σ(ρ) = U · diagonal(μ) · U⋆` for `μ = eigenvalues − ½` (using\n`U U⋆ = 1`).  Conjugation preserves trace and determinant, so the two\nproved invariants `fai_projector_sigma_trace` (`tr σ(ρ) = 0`) and\n`fai_projector_sigma_det` (`det σ(ρ) = −¼`) give `μ₀ + μ₁ = 0` and\n`μ₀ μ₁ = −¼`; hence `{μ₀, μ₁} = {½, −½}`.  In the case `μ = (½, −½)`,\n`diagonal μ = σ₀` and `u = U`; in the case `μ = (−½, ½)`,\n`diagonal μ = P σ₀ P` for the swap permutation `P = !![0,1;1,0]`\n(unitary), and `u = U · P`.  Either way `σ(ρ) = u · σ₀ · star u`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_sigma_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_sigma_det","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L144-L168","doc":"**Orbit invariant — determinant of the traceless component.**  For a\nrank-1 projector `ρ` on `ℂ²`, `det σ(ρ) = −¼`, matching `det σ₀ = −¼`.\nTogether with `tr σ(ρ) = 0` this fixes both coefficients of the\ncharacteristic polynomial `t² − (tr)·t + det = t² − ¼`, so every\n`σ(ρ)` has the same char poly as `σ₀` (eigenvalues `±½`).  Since a\nHermitian matrix is unitarily diagonalisable and its char poly\ndetermines its spectrum, this is exactly the statement that the\n`σ`-image of `ℙ(V)` is a *single* `U(2)`-adjoint orbit — the\nconjugacy step below.\n\nStated over a generic characteristic-zero field per §7c (the `½`, `¼`\nneed `2` invertible); `_orbit` specialises it to `ℂ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_sigma_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_sigma_trace","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L128-L142","doc":"**Orbit invariant — trace of the traceless component.**  For any\nrank-1 projector `ρ` (`tr ρ = 1`), the traceless component\n`σ(ρ) = ρ − ½·id` has `tr σ(ρ) = 0` — it lands in `Ad(A) = 𝔰𝔲(2)`\n(the traceless Hermitian matrices), as the manuscript's `σ` requires.\nMatches `tr σ₀ = 0`.\n\nThe `½` needs `2` invertible, so per §7c this is stated over a generic\ncharacteristic-zero field `[Field R] [CharZero R]` (the natural setting\nfor `σ(ρ) ∈ 𝔰𝔲(2)`); `_orbit` specialises it to `ℂ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.smul_one_diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.smul_one_diag","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L121-L126","doc":"Helper: a scalar multiple of the identity is the constant diagonal\nmatrix, `c • 1 = diagonal (fun _ => c)`.  Used to split `σ(ρ)` through\nthe spectral decomposition of `ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.sigmaBasePoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.sigmaBasePoint","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L115-L119","doc":"The base point `σ₀ = ½·diag(1, −1)` of the coadjoint orbit: the\ntraceless component `σ(ρ₀) = ρ₀ − ½·id` of the base rank-1\nprojector `ρ₀ = diag(1, 0)` on `τ(V) = ℂ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_det_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_det_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L92-L113","doc":"**Orbit invariant — determinant.**  A rank-1 projector `ρ` on\n`τ(V) = ℂ²` (idempotent `ρ² = ρ` with `tr ρ = 1`, so its eigenvalues\nare `1, 0`) has `det ρ = 0`.  Pure `Fin 2` entry algebra: the `(0,0)`\nentry of `ρ² = ρ` gives `ρ₀₀² + ρ₀₁ρ₁₀ = ρ₀₀`, and the trace gives\n`ρ₀₀ + ρ₁₁ = 1`; then `det ρ = ρ₀₀ρ₁₁ − ρ₀₁ρ₁₀ = 0` by\n`linear_combination`.  (This is the archimedean shadow of \"a rank-1\nprojector is singular\"; it fixes one of the two char-poly invariants\nthat pin the coadjoint orbit.)\n\nPurely algebraic (no archimedean structure), so per AGENTS.md §7c it\nis stated over a generic `[CommRing R]`; the `ℂ` orbit lives in the\n`_orbit` corollary below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit_matrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit_matrix","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L83-L90","doc":"The concrete 2-dimensional instance: a projector `ρ` on the\nstandard representation `V ≅ ℝ²` (as a `2 × 2` real matrix)\nsatisfies `(2ρ - 1)² = 1`, where `1` is the identity matrix\n`id_V`.  Immediate from the generic ring statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L69-L81","doc":"**Lemma** ([`lem:fai-projector-coadjoint-orbit`], involution part) —\nresolving declaration for the `lean.ref` URI\n`qou:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit`.\n\nFor any idempotent `ρ` in a ring, `(2ρ - 1)² = 1`: the doubled\ntraceless component of a projector is an involution.  Proved\nsorry-free via `twice_sigma_sq_eq_one`; the coadjoint-orbit\nidentification `ℙ(V) ≅ G/T` of the `.md` statement is stated\n(with a cited `sorry`) as `fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit_orbit`\nbelow. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:fai-projector-coadjoint-orbit","label":"lem:fai-projector-coadjoint-orbit","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/fai-projector-coadjoint-orbit.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.twice_sigma_sq_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.twice_sigma_sq_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/fai_projector_coadjoint_orbit.lean#L51-L67","doc":"**Involution identity for projectors** — if `ρ` is idempotent\n(`ρ * ρ = ρ`) in a (not necessarily commutative) ring, then\n`(2ρ - 1)² = 1`.\n\nThis is the algebraic core of\n[`lem:fai-projector-coadjoint-orbit`]: writing\n`σ(ρ) = ρ - ½·id_V` for the traceless component of a rank-1\nprojector on the categorical-dimension-2 standard representation,\n`2σ(ρ) = 2ρ - 1` and the claim `(2σ(ρ))² = id_V` is exactly this\nidentity.  Proof: expand `(2ρ - 1)² = 4ρ² - 4ρ + 1` (numerals are\ncentral, so `noncomm_ring` normalises), rewrite `ρ² = ρ`, and the\nlinear terms cancel. ","signatureChunk":0}]}